# AgentDesk

Local-first Elixir/Phoenix desktop app. Specs are in `docs/`. Working rules are in `AGENTS.md`.

Read `docs/README.md`, then the spec that matches the change (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DB.md`, `docs/A2A.md`, `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, `docs/PROVIDERS.md`, `docs/SECURITY.md`, `docs/PLAN.md`). Do not contradict `docs/DECISIONS.md`.

- LiveView renders; OTP orchestrates; SQLite is canonical; PubSub is ephemeral.
- Provider details stay in `AgentDesk.Providers.*`. A2A stays in `AgentDesk.A2A.*`.
- Agents talk to the hub through MCP, never peer sockets or the database.
- Canonicalize paths. Leases go through `ResourceManager`. No permanent lock files.
- Bind listeners to loopback. Never store provider secrets in SQLite.
- Isolated mode must not edit the user's primary worktree.
- Mutating A2A calls need an idempotency key. Registry keys are strings/UUIDs, never `String.to_atom/1`.
